Use the Sega 6-button pad layout for the Saturn Control Pad.

The Saturn pad is two rows of three: A B C on the bottom, X Y Z above.
The primary row belongs across the face buttons of a modern pad and the
secondary row on top:

    Saturn        RetroPad
    X  Y  Z       L   X   R
    A  B  C       Y   B   A

This is the layout Genesis Plus GX uses for the Mega Drive 6-button pad,
which is the same physical arrangement, and it is what REG-Linux applies
across every Saturn backend (lr-yabasanshiro, lr-beetle-saturn and the
mednafen "ss" module) so the buttons do not move when you switch
emulator.

The stock mapping put A/B on the B/A diamond and left C on a shoulder,
splitting the primary row.

The ST-V JAMMA key configs (stv_key_config / stv6b_key_config) keep the
arcade layout and are deliberately untouched.

